  "docTitle": "Distributed Configuration Service - SDE Prep Dojo",
  "description": "Design a configuration and feature-flag service that pushes updates to thousands of microservices: versioning, watch and long-poll, client caching with last-known-good, staged rollout and automatic rollback, consistency, audit and access control. Compared with ZooKeeper, etcd and AWS AppConfig.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n        <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n          <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"4\">Level 4 - Advanced</span>\n          <span class=\"time\">40 min</span>\n          <span class=\"chip accent\">HLD design</span>\n          <span class=\"chip company\">Microsoft</span>\n        </div>\n        <h1>Distributed Configuration Service</h1>\n        <p class=\"lead\">Design the service that tells thousands of running services \"the timeout is now 800 ms\" or \"turn the new checkout on for 5% of users\", within seconds, without a redeploy, and without one bad change taking the whole company down. You will learn versioning, watches and long-polling, last-known-good caching, staged rollout with automatic rollback, and the small client component interviewers ask you to code.</p>\n      "
  },
